# Pump encoding, BFO (pins: BFO-ontology/BFO-2020 @ dd89f4a, temporalized
# relations profile).
#
# R1: continuant parthood by the temporalized pair. The profile ships
# "proper continuant part of at some time" (BFO_0000175) and "continuant
# part of at all times" (BFO_0000177). The temporal index is fused into
# the relation's name, so the one assertion below is the profile's entire
# expressive reach for R1: the impeller, replaced at maintenance, is a
# proper part at some time and not at all times -- and the maintenance
# interval itself cannot be named by either relation. The thinness of
# this file is the finding, not an omission.
#
# Declarations repeat the pinned artifact's typing so the file renders
# correctly on its own (in Protege, undeclared properties display as
# annotations); semantics come only from the artifact at the pin.
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix obo: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix p:   <https://example.org/mt-pump#> .

obo:BFO_0000030 a owl:Class .          # object
obo:BFO_0000175 a owl:ObjectProperty . # proper continuant part of at some time

p:impeller a obo:BFO_0000030 ;
    obo:BFO_0000175 p:pump .           # proper continuant part of at some time
p:pump a obo:BFO_0000030 .

# R2: the impeller-housing joint is inexpressible. The 2020 standard and
# its OWL profiles carry no connection relation (the earlier
# boundary-and-connection apparatus is absent from the standard); the
# ecosystem's adjacent_to lives in RO, outside the standard.
